Here's a simple Java program that prints a square diamond pattern with '*' characters.

```java
public class DiamondPattern {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 5; // size of the diamond
        printDiamond(n);
    }

    public static void printDiamond(int n) {
        // Print the upper half of the diamond
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            // Print spaces before the stars
            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
                System.out.print(" ");
            }
            // Print stars
            for (int k = 0; k <= i; k++) {
                System.out.print("* ");
            }
            System.out.println();
        }

        // Print the lower half of the diamond
        for (int i = n - 2; i >= 0; i--) {
            // Print spaces before the stars
            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
                System.out.print(" ");
            }
            // Print stars
            for (int k = 0; k <= i; k++) {
                System.out.print("* ");
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}
```

This program works by first printing the upper half of the diamond, then the lower half. The number of spaces before the stars decreases by one for each row, and the number of stars increases by one for each row. The result is a diamond shape with '*' characters.

