Create a stored procedure that takes the user's input query as a parameter. This stored procedure will check if the query contains any blacklisted keywords.

```sql
CREATE PROCEDURE ValidateQuery
    @Query NVARCHAR(255)
AS
BEGIN
    DECLARE @QueryText NVARCHAR(255) = @Query;
    DECLARE @BlacklistedKeyword NVARCHAR(255);

    DECLARE cur CURSOR FOR
    SELECT Keyword
    FROM BlacklistedKeywords;

    OPEN cur;

    FETCH NEXT FROM cur INTO @BlacklistedKeyword;

    WHILE @@FETCH_STATUS = 0
    BEGIN
        IF CHARINDEX(@BlacklistedKeyword, @Query) > 0
        BEGIN
            RAISERROR('Invalid query', 16, 1);
            CLOSE cur;
            DEALLOCATE cur;
